const EN={brand:'Agricultural observatory',eyebrow:'BOLIVIA · AGRICULTURAL CENSUS 2013',title:'Animal populations,<br>municipality by municipality.',lead:'Explore absolute counts for 28 animal categories across 339 municipalities. Original census values and municipality names are preserved.',municipalities:'Municipalities',categories:'Animal categories',explore:'Explore the counts',animal:'Animal or category',measure:'Measure',mapDownload:'Download SVG map',mapSource:'Source: INE, CNA2013. Geometry: GeoBolivia / DS4Bolivia, 2015 reference, via geo4bolivia (Carlos Méndez and collaborators). Operational link; exact 2013/2015 boundary equivalence unverified.',selectPlace:'Select a municipality on the map or table',largest:'Largest values',native:'Native counts CSV',linked:'Counts + map CSV',crosswalk:'Crosswalk',dictionary:'Dictionary',rates:'Rates and components',denominators:'Denominators',controls:'Published controls',table:'Municipal data',tableHint:'Sorted by full reference code. On mobile, scroll the table horizontally.',code:'Reference code',department:'Department',province:'Province',municipality:'Municipality',count:'Absolute count',upas:'All UPAs',estimated:'Estimated residents 2013',plantsTitle:'What else can we study?',cropsTitle:'Crops, areas and harvests',cropsText:'The crop workbook contains products, codes and groups, irrigated/rainfed hectares and harvests in quintales. Seasons and associated crops must be reviewed before summing areas. These measure area and production, not numbers of plants.',treesTitle:'Fruit trees and medicinal plants',treesText:'The dictionary includes counts of scattered fruit plants. Medicinal plants are recorded by species, without a plant-count field in that entity. Redatam records and links still require validation.',equipmentTitle:'Infrastructure and machinery',equipmentText:'Tractors, equipment, silos, greenhouses and land use already have municipal columns. Equipment counts differ from owning UPAs. Land totals and their components must not be added together.',otherTitle:'Water, energy, labour and credit',otherText:'Candidates for later products. Productive water and energy use do not measure household services; family labour aged 8+ is not the whole population. Every variable needs its own universe and period.',catalog:'Variable catalogue',cropInventory:'Observed crops',priorities:'Exploration and priorities',peru:'Diagnostic and Peru',methodTitle:'Sources and interpretation',methodCounts:'All 9,492 published animal counts are preserved without imputation. The bovino field excludes oxen and agrees with INE table 62; oxen remain separate. No indiscriminate sum across all categories is offered.',methodMap:'The crosswalk preserves 339 source keys and 339 polygons. Six name-based links were corroborated using administrative hierarchy and location. This identifies municipalities; it does not certify equal historical boundaries. Census names remain visible.',methodRates:'Secondary views: heads/all UPAs, including UPAs without the species. This is not mean herd size among owners. Residents2013 = P2012 + (P2024 − P2012)/12: a linear census-year convention, not observed population or an official projection. Calculations retain decimals. The population baseline inherits explicit territorial allocations for changed 2024 municipalities.',methodLimits:'Published farm-bird controls are rounded to thousands with one decimal and group four species; they do not independently certify every head in each category. Published zeros are preserved; original imputation was not reconstructed. Plant exploration does not yet produce new municipal indicators.',questionnaireLimit:'The questionnaire was located, but download/visual inspection was unavailable. Questions were reviewed through the preserved Redatam dictionary. This verification limit is documented.',readme:'Method and reproduction',bibliography:'Bibliography',credits:'Design adapted from the local population product and geo4bolivia. Data: Instituto Nacional de Estadística. Geometry: GeoBolivia / DS4Bolivia. Author: Favio Leiva.'};
Object.assign(EN,{title:'The agricultural census,<br><em>municipality by municipality.</em>',lead:'Explore 86 variables: animals, agricultural land, irrigation, forests, machinery, infrastructure, family labour and holdings across 339 municipalities.',categories:'Available variables',explore:'Explore the variables',animal:'Variable',topic:'Topic',otherDownload:'Other variables + map CSV',otherNative:'Other native variables CSV',otherDictionary:'Other variable definitions',plantsTitle:'Plants and variables still pending',equipmentText:'Explore these figures using the Topic selector. Equipment and structures are counted as items, land in hectares. Equipment is not owning holdings; land totals and components must not be added together.',methodLimits:'Farm-bird controls are rounded and group four species. Published zeros are preserved; original imputation was not reconstructed. Published municipal land areas are now visible; detailed crop indicators and Redatam plant records still require processing and validation.'});
